---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy policy for Ancient China Wonder — minimal data, no advertising cookies, no cross-site tracking, cookieless aggregate analytics.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:28px;">
        <p><em>Last updated: October 2026.</em></p>
        <p>
          This site is a static website run by an independent hobbyist. It is designed to collect as
          little information as possible. In plain language:
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Newsletter email address.</strong> If you subscribe, your email address is stored by our mailing-list provider (Buttondown) solely to send you the newsletter. Every email contains a one-click unsubscribe link; unsubscribing deletes your address from the list.</li>
          <li><strong>Cookie preference.</strong> A single item in your browser's local storage records whether you accepted or declined the cookie notice. It never leaves your device.</li>
          <li><strong>Anonymous visit counts.</strong> We use Vercel Web Analytics, built into our host (Vercel), to count page views. It is cookieless, stores no personal data and cannot identify you — it records only aggregate, anonymous metrics such as page path, referrer domain and country.</li>
          <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> Our hosting provider (Vercel) keeps standard, short-lived technical logs (IP address, user agent, pages requested) for security and abuse prevention. We do not access, combine or analyse these for profiling.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What we do not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No advertising cookies, tracking pixels or cross-site tracking.</li>
          <li>No Google Analytics and no third-party analytics service; the only measurement is our host's cookieless, aggregate page-view counter.</li>
          <li>No user accounts, no comment systems, no forms other than the newsletter signup.</li>
          <li>No selling, renting or sharing of any personal data with anyone.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Your rights (GDPR)</h2>
        <p>
          If you are in the EU/EEA, you have the right to access, correct, export or erase any personal
          data we hold about you — which, in practice, means your newsletter email address. Write to the
          address on the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> and it will be handled within thirty days.
          The legal basis for processing is your explicit consent, given at signup and revocable at any
          time via the unsubscribe link.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted by Vercel, and its built-in Web Analytics is the only visitor-measurement
          tool we use; it is cookieless and collects no personal data. The site loads fonts from Google
          Fonts, which involves a request to Google's servers. If this concerns you, browser extensions
          that block third-party fonts will not affect readability beyond a change of typeface. The
          newsletter form submits directly to Buttondown; their privacy policy applies to that submission.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
